<%# Archived stocks.

    What this section was: every archived stock, in a table identical to the active one, with no date,
    no explanation, and an **empty actions column** - because StockPolicy#show_trading_link? withholds
    trading on an archived stock unless the viewer holds it. So for almost every reader it was a price
    list of things they cannot buy, sitting under the list of things they can.

    What it is actually for: **a student who holds an archived stock has to be able to sell it.** That
    is the only action the data supports, and it is the only part worth putting on screen by default.
    The rest is oversight, so it goes behind a native disclosure - open it and it costs nothing until
    then. A teacher keeps access, which matters because a teacher is not an admin and has no other
    view of archived stocks.

    Nothing purges these. `archived` is a bare boolean with no archived_at, and no job deletes or
    ages them, so the list only grows - see design-todo for the retention question, which needs a
    column before it can be answered. %>
<% held = stocks.select { |stock| current_user.holding?(stock) } %>
<% rest = stocks - held %>

<% if held.any? %>
  <%= render "stocks/stocks_table",
             title: "Archived stocks you hold",
             stocks: held %>
<% end %>

<% if rest.any? %>
  <%# A native <details>, which design.md names as the disclosure pattern here - it opens with no
      JavaScript, and the marker is hidden because the chevron carries the state. %>
  <details class="group" data-testid="archived-stocks">
    <summary class="inline-flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-2 rounded-lg text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <%= lucide_icon "chevron-right", class: "size-4 shrink-0 text-slate-600 transition-transform group-open:rotate-90" %>
      Archived stocks (<%= rest.size %>)
    </summary>

    <div class="mt-3">
      <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
        These companies are no longer trading here, so they cannot be bought.
      </p>
      <%= render "stocks/stocks_table", title: nil, stocks: rest %>
    </div>
  </details>
<% end %>
